      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 800,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "## cleanup: prefix guard\nA phone_prefix must match ^\\d{8,}$ (digits only, 8+), or the request is refused with prefix_too_short before anything is deleted.",
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000040",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        900,
        240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1900,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## cleanup: Calendar and Sheets\nEach of the four parts (Calendar events, Sheets rows, inbound_messages, n8n_chat_histories) continues on error, so one failing part doesn't block the others; a failed part reports null. Calendar and Sheets match the prefix with a literal, case-sensitive startsWith/substring check in a Filter node, never a pattern built from the prefix. The Calendar search spans now to config.limits.max_booking_days_ahead plus a day, so it reaches every booking the assistant could make. Sheets rows are deleted one at a time by row_number descending, so a deletion can't shift the rows still queued. For Calendar and Sheets, three inputs feed one Aggregate (Always Output Data, so zero matches counts as 0): a delete's success and error outputs, tagged ok:true/ok:false, and the search-failure tag; count-cleanup-outcomes reduces it to one count, or null if any outcome failed, so exactly one item per part reaches the merge chain.",
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000041",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        900,
        1120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1900,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## cleanup: Postgres and result\nThe two Postgres deletes use starts_with($1), never LIKE, which a prefix like \"________\" would turn into a wildcard that deletes every row. Each continues on error into a null count. The merge chain adds both counts to the Calendar and Sheets result, and ok is true only when all four parts succeed.",
        "color": 5
      }
    }
